# Who must review a change before it can reach main.
# GitHub asks these teams for a review automatically, and branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners")
# makes that review mandatory. The teams are created in docs/security/github-settings.md, step 2.
#
#   @lion-business-services/maintainers       the people who work on the code
#   @lion-business-services/security-owners   the people who answer for security and for commercial terms
#
# The LAST matching line wins, so the general rule comes first and the sensitive paths after it.
# Until the two teams exist, GitHub shows this file as having errors and asks nobody: create the teams first.

*                                       @lion-business-services/maintainers

# The database: every table, every access rule, every function. A mistake here crosses company boundaries.
/supabase/                              @lion-business-services/security-owners

# Server functions: sign-in, sessions, secrets, integrations, webhooks.
/api/                                   @lion-business-services/security-owners

# Browser protections and hosting settings.
/vercel.json                            @lion-business-services/security-owners
/Dockerfile                             @lion-business-services/security-owners
/.dockerignore                          @lion-business-services/security-owners
/deploy/                                @lion-business-services/security-owners

# The checks themselves, so a change cannot weaken a check and pass it in the same pull request unseen.
/.github/                               @lion-business-services/security-owners
/.gitleaks.toml                         @lion-business-services/security-owners
/scripts/security/                      @lion-business-services/security-owners
/scripts/backup/                        @lion-business-services/security-owners
/tests/security/                        @lion-business-services/security-owners
/supabase/tests/                        @lion-business-services/security-owners

# Security documents and the list of settings.
/SECURITY.md                            @lion-business-services/security-owners
/docs/security/                         @lion-business-services/security-owners
/docs/SECURITY.md                       @lion-business-services/security-owners
/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md                     @lion-business-services/security-owners
/.env.example                           @lion-business-services/security-owners

# Prices and plan contents: changed only with the owner's approval.
/config/vyntex-build-pricing.json       @lion-business-services/security-owners

# Libraries: a new or changed dependency is code that runs with the platform's access.
/package.json                           @lion-business-services/security-owners
/package-lock.json                      @lion-business-services/security-owners
